// Reviewed Steam 53.17 instruction contexts. The resolver admits these only
// for the exact image digest selected by ui_settings_tail_shift(). The two
// Arena pickers have similar drawing bodies; their distinct filter calls and
// query-to-owner offsets establish the identities below. The character mouse
// handler's six rich-text calls retain their source/box pairs while its sheet
// moves from R13 to RDI; native_rich_profile.inc owns those opcode signatures.
// The generic reading handler retains its instruction layout but has an
// embedded RVA switch table. Admit only the required call instructions here.
// Pause/settings bodies changed around their unchanged entry stores. The
// world-generation body retains its positions while init atlas offsets and
// its trailing switch table move; bind only the consumed entry and returns.
// Journal/caption and legends switch targets retain their control flow; only
// consumed instruction/return spans are admitted. History RTTI names and every
// slot retain their ABI. Global members are backed by exact RIP references.
// Map clear/update_all retain their complete entry instructions. Each action,
// justice and tracking caller below has a unique 96-byte instruction context; only
// its captured return address is consumed. Tracking fields retain their
// flags, nine-position array and 16-byte spoor-record layout.
// Four top-bar calls have unique 96-byte original instruction contexts.
// Their cursor/color callees keep the same argument ABI and are bound apart.
// Designation, petition, look-list and embark calls retain unique local
// instruction contexts and the same callees. Repeated designation cells need
// up to 192 bytes to distinguish them. The petition successor keeps its full
// seven-byte CMP; only its RIP operand changes. Arena weather's open flag is
// identified by the CMP and object LEA in a unique 320-byte renderer context.
// The seven zero-count HUD writers retain unique addst return contexts.
// HUD panel open bytes are corroborated by multiple independent RIP owners.
// Metal resource rows retain the material +0x260 name, capitalization and
// addst argument sequence in all three lists, including each wrap branch.
// Bind those consumed returns explicitly; their repeated local bodies cannot
// independently distinguish the world-generation and travel-map writers.
// The accepted-petition list keeps its six addst sources at rbp+0x3550
// through rbp+0x3610: guild request/recipient/date, then faith equivalents.
// Bind their returns separately from the skin/iterator calls so the private
// layer retains each complete field's identity after the renderer moves.
